.TH GF-STUDY 1 "November 2026" "GridForge 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gf-study \- GridForge, the meshing and simulation workbench, without a window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gf-study mesh
.I part
.B \-\-size
.I H
.RB [ \-\-order " " \fIN\fR]
.RB [ \-\-through\-wall " " \fIN\fR]
.RB [ \-o " " \fIDIR\fR]
.RB [ \-\-pvd ]
.RB [ \-\-inp ]
.br
.B gf-study deck
.I setup part
.B \-\-size
.I H
.RB [ \-\-order " " \fIN\fR]
.RB [ \-\-through\-wall " " \fIN\fR]
.RB [ \-o " " \fIDIR\fR]
.br
.B gf-study solve
.I setup part
.B \-\-size
.I H
.RB [ \-\-order " " \fIN\fR]
.RB [ \-\-through\-wall " " \fIN\fR]
.B \-o
.I JOB
.br
.B gf-study convert
.IR job.frd | mesh.msh
.RB [ \-\-deck " " \fIFILE\fR]
.RB [ \-\-pvd ]
.RB [ \-o " " \fIDIR\fR]
.br
.B gf-study converge
.I setup part
.B \-\-size
.I H
.RB [ \-\-ratio " " \fIR\fR]
.B \-o
.I DIR
.br
.B gf-study compare
.I results.vtkhdf test.vtp
.B \-\-force\-on
.I GROUP
.B \-\-gauge
.I POINTS
.RB [ \-\-times " " \fIN\fR]
.RB [ \-o " " \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B gf-study mesh-worker
.I part
.B \-\-recipe
.I JSON
.B \-o
.I mesh.vtu
.SH DESCRIPTION
The same work as the GridForge window, from the command line.
.PP
A
.I part
is a STEP file or a .brep (as FreeCAD's exportBrep writes it, in mm). A
.I setup
is a study.json, or a file holding its "setup".
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B mesh
The part's solids meshed with tetrahedra, each solid and face as a set,
written as one .vtkhdf for ParaView, with a report of the mesh's quality.
.TP
.B deck
A CalculiX job from a set-up: mesh.inp and the deck around it.
.TP
.B solve
The set-up solved by its toolkit, the results in JOB/results.
.TP
.B convert
CalculiX results (job.frd) to one .vtkhdf for ParaView, the deck's named
sets as blocks; or a Gmsh mesh (mesh.msh) likewise, its physical groups
as the sets.
.TP
.B converge
The set-up solved on three meshes, each finer than the last by
\-\-ratio (default 1.5) in every size the recipe makes, in DIR/mesh-1 to
mesh-3; then how far the largest displacement and the largest von Mises
stress can be trusted against the mesh: converging (with its order, its
value at zero element size and the grid convergence index of Celik et
al. 2008), oscillating, or not converging (a sharp corner, or a load on
an edge or a point). Also written to DIR/convergence.json.
.TP
.B compare
Measured against predicted: a solve's force on a group (\-\-force-on,
times \-\-times N for a model that is 1/N of the test piece by symmetry)
against the strain of a virtual extensometer between two points of the
part (\-\-gauge "x,y,z;x,y,z"), beside a test's curve as TenSense
analysed it (its .vtp); the largest and mean differences in words, every
point in the CSV given with \-o.
.TP
.B mesh-worker
What the window runs to mesh, in a process of its own, so that a crash in
the mesher cannot close the window and Stop ends the meshing at once. The
part is meshed by the mesh step's parameters as study.json keeps them
(\-\-recipe '{"maxSize": 3, "order": 2}'), and the mesh written to one
.vtu holding every value exactly, with its sets and provenance. If it
cannot, the reason is the last line on standard error, and the exit code
is 1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-size " H"
The largest element edge, in the geometry's units.
.TP
.BI \-\-order " N"
1 (straight edges, the default) or 2 (a middle node on each edge, on the
geometry).
.TP
.BI \-\-through\-wall " N"
Elements through a thin wall (default 2; 0: none added). A wall (a face
at least four times as wide as the wall behind it is thick) is meshed at
its thickness over N + 1, where that is finer than \-\-size.
.TP
.BI \-\-refine " GROUP=SIZE"
A group of faces meshed finer, its largest element there (deck, solve,
converge); repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-ratio " R"
converge: how much finer each mesh is than the last (default 1.5; at
least 1.3).
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-out " DIR"
Write into DIR (default: beside the input).
.TP
.BI \-\-deck " FILE"
Read the named sets from FILE (default: job.inp beside the results, if
there is one).
.TP
.B \-\-pvd
Write a .vtu series and its .pvd instead (no sets).
.TP
.B \-\-inp
mesh: also write the mesh and its sets as <name>.inp, for a CalculiX deck
to *INCLUDE.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and the build.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GF_CCX
The ccx to solve with; else the one beside the CalculiX toolkit's
adapter, else ccx on PATH.
.TP
.B GF_MESH_TRACE
When set, a fingerprint after each of the mesher's stages, on standard
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR GridForge (1)
